---

These examples enumerate a three-unit SRSWOR, expose what zero pair support
does and does not permit, check the one-unit and census boundaries, and show
how a valid unbiased Sen–Yates–Grundy estimate can be negative for one sample
even while the true design variance remains nonnegative.
